### Why

The former customized Codex checkout combined source patches, runtime helpers,
Nix packaging, release mutation, and consumer installation. The public
`loiang/co` fork needs a source-built, CLI-only lifecycle that can merge fixed
upstream commits without rewriting history and can prove the exact candidate
works with ni's independently pinned official Code Mode host.

### Goal

Keep customized Codex on `main`, merge upstream into isolated upgrade
worktrees, publish only evidence-bound CLI assets, and make consumer updates
explicit and compare-and-swap protected. Keep the official host and all secret
lifecycle operations outside this repository.

### Accomplished

#### Source customization

- Preserved the customized bundled-skills removal and StateDbOnly resume picker
  behavior on the current official Codex source baseline.
- Added native `/archive-except <thread-id>` handling. The selected thread, its
  ancestors, and its descendants are protected while eligible sibling
  subtrees can be archived; the TUI includes confirmation, progress, and
  completion/error handling.
- Retained the migrated `codex-archive-subagents` runtime helper, while removing
  the obsolete Niko and `codex-auth` entry points. Codex authentication data is
  now managed by ni's `secret` lifecycle.

#### Build and lifecycle

- Added static-musl Codex CLI packaging, Cargo lock/vendor hashing, flake checks,
  release layout checks, and deterministic CLI asset/manifest generation. The
  official Code Mode host is neither compiled nor published here; ni owns and
  pins that host independently.
- Added repository lifecycle entry points for upstream merge worktrees,
  conflict finalization, scoped tests, local builds, real host compatibility,
  publication, local main fast-forward promotion, and explicit ni-backed
  installation.
- Upgrade fixes the upstream SHA, uses merge rather than rebase, preserves a
  conflicted worktree for continuation, refreshes only required Cargo git
  hashes/Nix lock nodes, and never force-pushes.
- Publication binds source, lock, build, test, and host evidence to one clean
  commit; it updates remote `main` only by fast-forward and atomically pushes
  that ref with a new tag and optional notes. Existing tags and assets are
  rejected rather than overwritten.
- Installation resolves and builds the exact remote `main` or `co-*` tag,
  validates it against ni's pinned host before mutation, then uses ni's
  `--expected-rev` CAS update, lock checks, system build, and explicit
  `rebuild ... switch --no-update`.

#### Configuration and security boundary

- Migrated the tracked non-secret Codex, mgrep, upstream-baseline, weekly-limit,
  and billing-date configuration required by the fork.
- No authentication payload, private model access, or generated environment
  file is stored or consumed by this change.

